DESCRIPTION:Anything to correct since this morning? Correct it before 5 PM
 : "Actually\, that's not true. The truth is ___." Then log it tonight.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 1 Midday check
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-2@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T233011Z
DTSTART:20261029T210000
DTEND:20261029T211000
SUMMARY:Day 1 Evening Ledger
DESCRIPTION:Tonight's question: How many did you log? Which one surprised 
 you most\, and why?\n\nTHE LEDGER (10 min)\n1. Lies told today (#): what\,
  to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Corrections made (#)\n4. T
 he trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and the fear (failure / reject
 ion / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my head: "If I tell the tr
 uth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened when I told the truth\n
 7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then: "If ___\, then I'll say
  ___."\n8. One line of prayer or thanks
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 1 Evening Ledger
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-3@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T233011Z
DTSTART:20261030T063000
DTEND:20261030T063500
SUMMARY:Day 2 Morning: Name the kind
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nTag eac
 h lie today by type. COVER: hiding a mistake. INFLATE: looking better than
  you are. SMOOTH: avoiding conflict. AUTO: no reason at all\, it just came
  out.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'l
 l say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Most lies come from a small group of people. 
 Lying a lot is a pattern\, not human nature. Patterns can be counted and c
 hanged. That's why Week 1 is counting. (Serota\, Levine & Boster (2010)\, 
 Human Communication Research)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 2 Morning: Name the kind
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
