UID:truth-ledger-6@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T233011Z
DTSTART:20261031T063000
DTEND:20261031T063500
SUMMARY:Day 3 Morning: Build your corner
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nAction 
 before noon: ask the men who will be in your corner. 1) Your accountabilit
 y brother\, who gets your numbers every week. 2) Your witness: your pastor
  or an older man you respect\, who will hear your inventory and help you p
 repare to tell your wife. 3) A free group if one is near you\, like Celebr
 ate Recovery or a church men's group. If your job (or your wife's) has an 
 Employee Assistance Program\, call it today. Most offer a few free\, confi
 dential counseling sessions.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If
  ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Self-guided CBT can wo
 rk as well as sessions with a therapist. You can do this work without payi
 ng a counselor\, but not alone. The "guided" part matters: your brother\, 
 your witness and your group keep you from quitting. (Cuijpers et al. (2010
 )\, Psychological Medicine)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 3 Morning: Build your corner
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
