SUMMARY:Day 8 Morning: The fear of failing
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nEach time you feel the urge to lie today\, ask yourself: "Am I hiding
  that I failed?"\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens
 \, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Trying to look competent or likabl
 e makes people lie more. Your two fears\, failing and not being accepted\,
  are exactly these two goals. Week 2 teaches you to notice which one is ru
 nning in the moment. (Feldman\, Forrest & Happ (2002)\, Basic and Applied 
 Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 8 Morning: The fear of failing
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
