SUMMARY:Day 9 Morning: The fear of not being accepted
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nEach time the urge hits\, ask yourself: "Am I trying to be liked righ
 t now?"\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I
 'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Trying to look competent or likable makes p
 eople lie more. Your two fears\, failing and not being accepted\, are exac
 tly these two goals. Week 2 teaches you to notice which one is running in 
 the moment. (Feldman\, Forrest & Happ (2002)\, Basic and Applied Social Ps
 ychology)
