SUMMARY:Day 12 Morning: Test your prediction
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nRun an experiment. Before one hard truth today\, write your predictio
 n first: "If I say it\, ___ will happen." Then say it.\n\nBefore you go\, 
 write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it wor
 ks: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the truth is
  survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. The tru
 th ladder (Week 4) and the prediction test (Day 12) are behavioral experim
 ents. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis
 )
