SUMMARY:Day 14 Morning: Week 2 review: your Fear Map
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nToday\, draw your Fear Map: your top three fears\, the lie each one p
 roduces\, and the truth each one avoids. Share it with your witness.\n\nBe
 fore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."
 \n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you tha
 t the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of your predi
 ction. The truth ladder (Week 4) and the prediction test (Day 12) are beha
 vioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999
 )\; Salkovskis)
