SUMMARY:Day 15 Morning: The three-second pause
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nPractice the sequence: alarm\, breath\, "Give me a second." Use it at le
 ast once today\, even in a conversation that's easy.\n\nBefore you go\, wr
 ite today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works
 : The pause interrupts an automatic response. The three-second pause isn't
  magic. It's the gap where your prepared true sentence gets a chance. (Kob
 is et al. (2019)\, Perspectives on Psychological Science\; Curtis & Hart (
 2020))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 15 Morning: The three-second pause
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
