SUMMARY:Day 18 Morning: Write your if-then plans
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nWrite five if-then plans for your five most common lie situations: "If s
 he asks whether I finished it\, then I say exactly how far I got." "If som
 eone asks what I paid\, then I say the real number." Save them in your pho
 ne.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll 
 say ___."\n\nWhy it works: If-then plans work. Every morning you write one
  if-then plan for the day's risk moment: "If she asks about the money\, th
 en I'll say the real number." (Gollwitzer & Sheeran (2006)\, Advances in E
 xperimental Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 18 Morning: Write your if-then plans
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
