SUMMARY:Day 19 Morning: Slow down
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nIn every hard conversation today\, speak about 20% slower. Rushing feeds
  lies.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'
 ll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Break an automatic habit: notice it\, then r
 eplace it. Day 5 teaches you your body's alarm. The pause and a prepared t
 rue sentence are the replacement response. Your brother is the support. (B
 ate\, Malouff\, Thorsteinsson & Bhullar (2011)\, Clinical Psychology Revie
 w (meta-analysis))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 19 Morning: Slow down
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
