DTSTAMP:20261028T233011Z
DTSTART:20261117T063000
DTEND:20261117T063500
SUMMARY:Day 20 Morning: No rounding up
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nToday\, nothing gets inflated: not numbers\, times\, effort or stories. 
 Small lies make the brain's alarm quieter\, which makes the next lie bigge
 r. Exact is the goal.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ ha
 ppens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Small lies make bigger lies e
 asier. There's no such thing as a harmless small lie for you. Every exagge
 ration trains the slope. That's why Day 20 is "No rounding up." (Garrett\,
  Lazzaro\, Ariely & Sharot (2016)\, Nature Neuroscience)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 20 Morning: No rounding up
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
