SUMMARY:Day 24 Morning: Admit it first
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nBefore anyone finds out\, admit one small mistake today: 
 "That was me. I'll fix it."\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If 
 ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Shame hides. Guilt repa
 irs. Day 11 teaches you to turn shame sentences into guilt sentences. You 
 can repair something you did. You can't repair who you are. (Tangney & Dea
 ring\, Shame and Guilt (2002) and later reviews)
