SUMMARY:Day 27 Morning: Take the reaction
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nBefore a hard conversation today\, take two minutes to wr
 ite about why your faith or your children matter to you. Then\, when the t
 ruth gets a reaction (frustration\, hurt\, silence)\, don't defend\, expla
 in or lie again. Say: "You're right to feel that."\n\nBefore you go\, writ
 e today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: 
 Remembering your values makes you less defensive. Before a hard conversati
 on with your wife\, spend two minutes writing about why your faith or your
  children matter to you. Then go listen. (Sherman & Cohen (2002)\, Current
  Directions in Psychological Science)
