SUMMARY:Day 32 Morning: A real apology
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Repair. Telling the truth is the start. Repair is the 
 work.\n\nA real apology has five parts: what I did\, how it hurt you\, no 
 excuses\, what I'm doing about it\, and no demand to be forgiven. Draft on
 e.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll s
 ay ___."\n\nWhy it works: Trust after lying comes back slowly\, through ac
 tions. Set your expectations: this is a long road\, and words won't carry 
 you. Make small\, specific promises and keep them exactly (Day 40). Never 
 demand trust (Day 39). (Schweitzer\, Hershey & Bradlow (2006)\, Organizati
 onal Behavior and Human Decision Processes)
