SUMMARY:Day 34 Morning: Repair with action
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Repair. Telling the truth is the start. Repair is the 
 work.\n\nPick one lie you can repair with action: return the money\, keep 
 the promise\, finish the task. Do it today.\n\nBefore you go\, write today
 's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Shame h
 ides. Guilt repairs. Day 11 teaches you to turn shame sentences into guilt
  sentences. You can repair something you did. You can't repair who you are
 . (Tangney & Dearing\, Shame and Guilt (2002) and later reviews)
