SUMMARY:Day 38 Morning: Her anger isn't the enemy
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Transparency. Trust is rebuilt on boring days.\n\nIf s
 he's hurt or angry today\, it's the cost of what happened\, not an attack 
 on you. Before you talk\, take two minutes to remember what kind of husban
 d you've decided to be. Then stay in the room\, listen\, and don't argue a
 bout the facts.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\
 , then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Remembering your values makes you l
 ess defensive. Before a hard conversation with your wife\, spend two minut
 es writing about why your faith or your children matter to you. Then go li
 sten. (Sherman & Cohen (2002)\, Current Directions in Psychological Scienc
 e)
