SUMMARY:Day 39 Morning: Don't demand trust
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Transparency. Trust is rebuilt on boring days.\n\nDon'
 t ask "When are you going to trust me?" Research on trust after deception 
 shows it comes back slowly and through actions\, not words. Whether she tr
 usts you is her decision. Being consistent is yours.\n\nBefore you go\, wr
 ite today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works
 : Trust after lying comes back slowly\, through actions. Set your expectat
 ions: this is a long road\, and words won't carry you. Make small\, specif
 ic promises and keep them exactly (Day 40). Never demand trust (Day 39). (
 Schweitzer\, Hershey & Bradlow (2006)\, Organizational Behavior and Human 
 Decision Processes)
