SUMMARY:Day 40 Morning: Keep one small promise
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Transparency. Trust is rebuilt on boring days.\n\nMake
  one small\, specific promise with a time on it\, and keep it exactly.\n\n
 Before you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___
 ."\n\nWhy it works: If-then plans work. Every morning you write one if-the
 n plan for the day's risk moment: "If she asks about the money\, then I'll
  say the real number." (Gollwitzer & Sheeran (2006)\, Advances in Experime
 ntal Social Psychology)
