SUMMARY:Day 44 Morning: Your warning signs
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Write your relapse warning signs: short on sleep\, stressed\, money troubl
 e\, isolated\, skipping the ledger\, keeping "small" secrets\, rounding up
  again.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I
 'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Tired men have less self-control. Treat bei
 ng tired as a risk factor. Your evening ledger and your relapse warning si
 gns include sleep. (Barnes\, Schaubroeck\, Huth & Ghumman (2011)\, Organiz
 ational Behavior and Human Decision Processes)
